s founded in 2008 and is headquartered in Irving, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Dr. David Dean Halbert M.D. | Chairman, CEO & Founder | Age 69 | Compensation: $5.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $440K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $36K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $38K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Caris Life Sciences, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $6.6B market cap on $812M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 29% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 18-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $67M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 48% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 194% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.9394427857827787},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (71% sell ratio, net $25.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Healthcare \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"BTSG vs. CAI: Which Stock Should Value Investors Buy Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3026587/btsg-vs-cai-which-stock-should-value-investors-buy-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_3-3026587","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794238804.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Citigroup Forecasts Strong Price Appreciation for Caris Life Sciences (NASDAQ:CAI) Stock","